{"id": "EUVD-2026-86129", "enisaUuid": "40a18b2c-063b-39dc-a4b3-8ca78ed90f9a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblock: handle nogenerate/noverify properly in fs-integrity\n\nCheck the BIP_CHECK flags before generating or verifying PI information,\notherwise this can be incorrectly called for non-PI metadata and\ncause generation of incorrect metadata and crashed in the verification\nhandler.\n\nThe new behavior matches that of the block layer auto-generated\nmetadata.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:51:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b681c740e6d645f7d7477e9208db57917c6c0fbc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bf9a21e7bccfd8c35b440efd114c61cc9838a41"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4jwc-f9v9-q77h", "CVE-2026-93257"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3bde0fe4-c6eb-3e66-94aa-6c235597a44f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "50b4009a-f055-3232-91d1-64e125851e97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "5ca04872-2eba-3f7b-97f5-d9a355001aff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "a43b1bc6-543c-37e2-a607-f4a1305896d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0bde8a12b5540572a7fd6d2867bee6de15e4f289 <3bf9a21e7bccfd8c35b440efd114c61cc9838a41"}, {"id": "dc85e1a2-8109-34ec-a5ea-25c8c71fca30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0bde8a12b5540572a7fd6d2867bee6de15e4f289 <b681c740e6d645f7d7477e9208db57917c6c0fbc"}, {"id": "fdcd344b-f3d2-36a8-b2e8-f88379d374cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dab0e1ae-0862-3e6b-bdcc-76a094768663", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}